<h4 style="position:relative;margin-left:10pt;margin-top:20pt;">General description of the course</h4>

<p style="position:relative;margin-left:20pt;width:90%"> 
This course is quite essential for students who are interested in any topic related to algebra. Note that in today's
mathematics algebra is an inseparable part of other areas of mathematics such as  
geometry and topology. 
Which is why MAT 3143 is the prereqisite for several of our fourth year mathematics courses, 
including MAT4141, MAT4145, MAT4149, MAT4154, MAT4157, MAT4158, and MAT4166.
</p>

<h4 style="position:relative;margin-left:10pt;">Official Course Syllabus</h4>

<p style="position:relative;;margin-left:20pt;width:90%">Rings, polynomial rings, homomorphisms, quotient 
rings, Euclidean rings, principal rings, factorial rings, fields, extensions of fields, splitting field, 
finite fields. 
</p>

<h4 style="position:relative;margin-left:10pt;">Prerequisites</h4>

<p style="position:relative;margin-left:20pt;width:90%">The prerequisites for this course are 
MAT2141 and MAT2143.
</p>

